On Windows, stty recognized rows, cols and columns as settings, though
it cannot set the window size and its usage lists only size. The first
pass checked the following number without consuming it, so "stty rows
30" always failed with "invalid argument '30'", and "stty rows" with
nothing after it dereferenced a null pointer and crashed. Recognize only
size, so these are rejected as invalid arguments like other settings
the Windows build lacks.

--- a/coreutils/stty.c
+++ b/coreutils/stty.c
@@ -1008,17 +1008,11 @@
 
 static int find_param(const char *name)
 {
-	static const char params[] ALIGN1 =
-		"rows\0"    /* 1 */
-		"cols\0"    /* 2 */
-		"columns\0" /* 3 */
-		"size\0";    /* 4 */
-	int i = index_in_strings(params, name) + 1;
-	if (i == 0)
-		return 0;
-	if (i != 4)
-		i |= 0x80;
-	return i;
+	/* The window size cannot be set, so rows, cols and columns are
+	 * not settings: accepting them consumed no argument, and with
+	 * none following, dereferenced a null pointer.
+	 */
+	return strcmp(name, "size") == 0 ? param_size : 0;
 }
 #endif
 
